{{~##
   The generated implementation: one parse function and one load function per table, plus
   the accessor that loads them together and links the references.

   Parsing is split from loading so neither needs a goto. The parse function reads and
   allocates and returns false the moment something is wrong; the load function owns the
   file buffer and the cleanup.

   Reads do not check as they go. The reader's failure is sticky - the first read that
   runs out of data records why and the rest do nothing - so a record's twenty fields are
   twenty lines and the row loop asks once. The two places that do check mid-flight are
   the loops whose trip count came off the wire.

   Anything needing the model arrives already rendered from CView.
##~}}
